extraction_notes: |
  - category occ / occ_group psychic per the batch convention (modelled on
    mind-melter), although the book heads it "Zapper R.C.C." (printed 81) and
    "Zapper Psychic R.C.C." (printed 82). men_of_arms false: a Master Psychic
    stat block, not a Men of Arms heading; no hit point or S.D.C. formula is
    printed. No race_restrictions: the page says most Zappers are human (87%),
    with Elves 5%, Ogres 5% and 3% other human-like races - a distribution, not
    a restriction, and humans are the main case.
  - xp_table taken from the class brief (read off a render of printed 157).
  - Special abilities #1-4 (printed 81) keep the book''s numbering in their
    names because the book refers to them by number. #3''s mega-damage bolt,
    its ley line/nexus damage and range multipliers, and the Electrified Body
    Protection field are all folded into that one entry; none of it is a
    bonus the sheet can add.
  - Psionics (printed 82 #5): eight powers granted outright. Book "Telekinesis
    (super)" = catalog "Telekinesis (Super)"; book "Neuro-Strike" = catalog
    Mind Bleeder power "Neural Strike" (the Mind Bleeder''s own page, printed
    48, prints it "Neural Strike"). No first-level picks (powers_starting
    omitted); one minor Physical power at levels 2, 4, 6, 8, 10 and 12.
  - Electrokinesis: the book says "double normal range", not double strength.
    The catalog row cannot hold a per-class range multiplier, so it is stated
    in the Super Electrokinesis special ability and not modelled.
  - I.S.P. (printed 82 #6): 3D4x10 + M.E., +2D4+4 per level (cache "3D4xlO",
    the known digit fault; render confirms 3D4x10). Regained at 2/hour active,
    12/hour meditating or sleeping - special_abilities, not a schema field.
  - P.P.E. 2D6 (#8). Bonuses (#9): +2 initiative, +1 strike, +1 pull punch,
    +1 roll with impact, +4 vs horror factor, +1 vs possession. "Loves action
    and excitement" is flavour, not stored.
  - Ley line influence (printed 82): range and duration +50% within one mile of
    a ley line; duration, range and damage doubled within one mile of a nexus.
    The book says "the Zapper''s pyrokinetic and other psychic powers" - an
    apparent carry-over from the Burster text; read as his electrokinetic and
    other powers. Conditional on location - GM Notes.
  - Skills (printed 82): no language line is printed, so none is granted.
    "Read Sensory Equipment" is the catalog''s Sensory Equipment (Pilot
    Related, 30+10=40). "Body Building" is Body Building & Weight Lifting.
    Fixed skills fold the bonus into the catalog base (Basic Electronics
    30+25=55, Radio: Basic 45+10=55, Climbing 40+5=45). Hand to Hand: Expert
    may become Martial Arts, or Assassin if evil, for one "other" skill.
  - R.C.C. Related (printed 82-83): four, +1 at levels 4, 8 and 12. The CS
    soldier''s extra two from Military and Espionage are conditional - note
    only. Military "except Armorer" is the catalog''s Field Armorer &
    Munitions Expert. Science "Math only" taken as both Mathematics: Basic and
    Advanced (judgement, same reading as the Psi-Nullifier). Medical
    "Brewing" is the catalog''s Brewing (not Brewing: Medicinal). Espionage
    "Wilderness Survival only" - the catalog files that skill under
    Wilderness, so the grant is cross-category. Cowboy and Rogue: none.
  - Secondary: four, +1 at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12.
  - Equipment (printed 83): the non-CS package is stored; the CS Operative
    package is in GM Notes. "Travelling clothes" stored as one traveling
    clothes; "1D4 medium-sized sacks" as sack 1D4; "silver cross" as
    small-silver-cross; "language translator" as portable-language-translator;
    "distancing binoculars" as infrared-distancing-binoculars; "laser
    distancer" as pocket-laser-distancer. "Neuro-Mace or Electro-Stunner (see
    Rifts Lone Star)": no Electro-Stunner row exists, so the neural-mace is
    granted. E-clips: four for the rifle plus 1D4 for each of the two weapons
    of choice, stored as one e-clip entry of 2D4+4. The two weapons of choice
    enumerate generic energy pistols/rifles plus the submachine gun. Vehicle:
    none to start.
  - Money (printed 83): non-CS 1D6x1000 credits (cache "!D6xlOOO", the known
    digit fault; render confirms 1D6x1000) plus Black Market items worth
    3D4x100 credits (not stored). CS troops instead get quarters, keep and a
    1900 credit monthly salary, starting with one month''s pay - GM Notes.
  - Alignment: none required, leaning Principled/Scrupulous or
    Miscreant/Diabolic. Attribute requirements: none (high M.E. and I.Q. 8+
    suggested). Neither is a schema restriction.
---

## Lore

Zappers are the rarest and most dangerous of the physical psychics: where the Burster commands fire, the Zapper commands electricity and telekinetic force. With a thought he can cloak himself in crackling current, hurl mega-damage lightning and drain the power out of machines. Only a few thousand exist across North America, most often in the old Canadian territories and the northeast. The Coalition''s Psi-Battalion fields a surprising number of them, as does Free Quebec. Most are thrill seekers who lean on their powers and wits far more than on training or gear.

## GM Notes

**Power ladder** (Psyscape p.82): at first level the Zapper knows Electrokinesis (double normal range), Telekinesis (Super), Telekinetic Force Field, Telekinetic Acceleration Attack, Telekinetic Punch, and the Mind Bleeder powers Brain Scan, Neuro-Touch and Neural Strike. He adds one minor Physical power at levels 2, 4, 6, 8, 10 and 12.

**Ley line influence:** range and duration of his powers +50% within one mile (1.6 km) of a ley line; duration, range and damage doubled within one mile of a nexus. Electrical Aura''s mega-damage bolt has its own printed figures (4D6 M.D. and triple range on a ley line, 6D6 M.D. and quadruple range at a nexus).

**CS Operative equipment (instead of the non-CS package):** Coalition "Dead Boy" body armor, energy rifle and energy sidearm of choice with 4 extra E-clips each, survival knife, vibro-blade, two grenades, one non-energy weapon of choice, three signal flares, air filter and gas mask, tinted goggles, first-aid kit, utility belt, walkie-talkie, dress uniform, combat boots and canteen. Other weapons, vehicles, ammunition, rations, repair, and Psi-Battalion training and counselling are issued as needed at the commanding officer''s discretion; heavy weapons and vehicles are rarely assigned. CS pay replaces starting money: room, board and basics plus 1900 credits a month, starting with one month''s pay, in a shared four-person Psi-Battalion dormitory with a private bedroom/study.

**Non-CS extras:** Black Market items worth 3D4x100 credits beside the 1D6x1000 credits. Independent Zappers find steady work as bounty hunters, bodyguards, enforcers and mercenaries.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'zapper');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'zapper';

